    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0481" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.94/112</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Acting Secretary of State of a
                        Conversation With the Polish Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Potocki</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-27">November 27, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The only specific matter the Ambassador desired to mention had reference to the
                    agreement between Germany and Japan, which has been fully reported in the
                    newspapers. He desired to know whether we have received any information to the
                    effect that Poland is a party to the agreement or proposes to be a party to the
                    agreement, and I answered that question in the negative. He then said he wished
                    us to understand that is the correct answer, since Poland has no intention of
                    becoming complicated in the situation to which the agreement pertains. He said a
                    Rumanian Commission is now in Poland headed by the Rumanian Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs, and mentioned the close arrangement between the two countries to
                    cooperate for self-protection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">alton</hi>] M[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oore</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
